ACE: Not bad. Honestly, that was the hardest one.
Tyrone: Woah... I actually got through it.
Tyrone: But I want to know how it decided which path to take.
ACE: Behind the scenes, the "if" statement checked your condition. Since it was true, it ran that specific block of code.
ACE: The "else" and "else if" blocks were completely ignored. Java only ever takes one road.
ACE: And for the "switch", it just looked at the variable and jumped straight to the matching case.
Tyrone: So one condition wins, and the rest get skipped.
ACE: You've got it, buddy. That's control flow. You tell the program how to think.
ACE: And every slip you made along the way taught you something.
Tyrone: Okay... I think I could actually explain this to somebody.
